#!/bin/bash
# Remove the PATH symlink created by ./install. The plugin itself is removed with
# `omarchy plugin remove rocha.pasteimage`.

set -uo pipefail

DEST="$HOME/.local/bin/omarchy-pasteimage"

if [[ -L $DEST ]]; then
  rm -f "$DEST"
  echo "Removed $DEST"
  [[ -e $DEST.bak ]] && echo "Note: $DEST.bak is still there."
else
  echo "No symlink at $DEST"
fi

cat <<'NOTE'

If you also removed the plugin, run `hyprctl reload` to hand SUPER+V back to your
Hyprland config — the binding lives in Hyprland's runtime state, so it survives
until the next config reload.
NOTE
